  "limitations": "1) CBS PDFs on cbs.gov.il could not be fetched directly (WebFetch permission denied) — all figures rely on Israeli press quoting those PDFs. Where two outlets agreed, confidence is marked 'high'. 2) The CBS Table 2.2 ('aa' prices) only covers 18-22 largest cities; the 168-city database has many smaller localities for which no CBS *average price* exists — press figures cited for them (mostly Hoomy/Dirobot/Madlan) are listings-based estimates, not transaction means, and are clearly marked 'medium' or 'low' confidence. 3) Construction-input-index annual values for 2016-2018 (1.5%, 1.9%, 1.5%) come from secondary aggregator tables (Kantahome) and were not cross-verified against the original 119/xxxx CBS releases. 4) The 2026 figures are partial year (through April CPI release of 2026-05-15) and will revise. 5) Per-city YoY price-index numbers do NOT exist in CBS publications — CBS publishes price-index changes at *district* level only; the city-level prices cited are absolute means from Table 2.2, not index changes. 6) Construction starts/completions per city were already collected separately in cbs_latest_updates.json — this file focuses on the four price-related publication families requested."
